@startuml False-Positive Tests Analysis
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE

title **CRITICAL: False-Positive Tests (Always Pass)**

skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor<<falsepos>> #FFCDD2
    BorderColor<<falsepos>> #E53935
    BackgroundColor<<weak>> #FFE0B2
    BorderColor<<weak>> #FB8C00
    BackgroundColor<<good>> #C8E6C9
    BorderColor<<good>> #43A047
}

package "False-Positive Tests (Always Pass)" <<falsepos>> {
    rectangle "WebhookEventDispatcherTest.php\nLine 206" as fp1
    rectangle "AddressHashRestorationTest.php\nLine 383" as fp2
    rectangle "HelloWorldTest.php\nLines 20-23" as fp3
}

note right of fp1
    canRegisterMultipleHandlers()
    **$this->assertTrue(true);**
end note

note right of fp2
    testAddressHashRestoredBeforePaymentEvent()
    **$this->assertTrue(true);**
    Comment: "if no dispatch, still pass"
end note

note right of fp3
    testPhpUnitWorks()
    **$this->assertTrue(true, ...);**
    Bootstrap test, not real test
end note

package "Weak Assertions (Hidden in Mocks)" <<weak>> {
    rectangle "AddressHashRestorationTest.php\nLines 361-364" as weak1
}

note right of weak1
    Assertion hidden in willReturnCallback():
    ->willReturnCallback(function($e) ...
        $this->assertTrue(...);
        return $e;
    ...);
end note

package "Good Test Pattern" <<good>> {
    rectangle "ProperTest" as good1
}

note right of good1
    Arrange: Setup preconditions
    Act: Execute code under test
    Assert: Verify outcomes
    **$this->assertEquals(expected, actual);**
end note

note as N1
    **Impact of False-Positive Tests:**
    1. False sense of security
    2. Tests pass even when code is broken
    3. Code coverage numbers are misleading
    4. Bugs slip into production

    **Action Required:**
    - Replace assertTrue(true) with meaningful assertions
    - Or delete the tests entirely
    - Move assertions out of mock callbacks
end note

N1 .. fp3

@enduml
